# This repo is a pi *configuration*: extensions, agents, skills, docs and the
# decisions behind them. Everything a pi session GENERATES is ignored, because
# it is machine-written, changes on every run, and would bury the config it sits
# beside. The rule of thumb: if deleting it costs nothing but a re-run, ignore it.

# ---- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The real .env: the ONLY file here holding live credentials. Both keys are
# read from it (docs/adr/0042) — LITELLM_API_KEY for the litellm provider and
# LITELLM_MCP_KEY for the mcp.json gateway header. agent/.env.example IS
# committed, so the repo states which variables it needs without holding one.
# Losing this file means re-minting two keys from the gateway; losing a key to
# git history would mean rotating them under pressure.
agent/.env
agent/.env.*
!agent/.env.example
# NOTE: agent/mcp.json and agent/extensions/litellm.ts used to be ignored here,
# each because it hardcoded a key. Both now read from agent/.env, so both are
# committed — mcp.json via a "Bearer ${LITELLM_MCP_KEY}" placeholder. This is
# the change the old comment on litellm.ts anticipated: its doc comments always
# claimed LITELLM_API_KEY came from the environment, and now that is true.
# Credential stores. Empty right now, which is exactly why they are easy to
# commit by accident and then hard to notice when they fill up.
agent/auth.json
agent/models-store.json
# Never commit a backup of a config that may contain a key.
*.bak
*.orig-backup

# ---- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
# bun's lockfile is binary; the text lockfile is committed instead if present.
bun.lockb

# ---- Session and transcript data --------------------------------------------
# Full conversation transcripts. Large, constantly rewritten, and they contain
# whatever the agents happened to read — including file contents from anywhere
# on this machine.
agent/sessions/
agent/subagent-sessions/
agent/pi-blackhole/
# Plans are per-session working state keyed by session id, and the archive grows
# without bound. The decisions worth keeping end up in docs/adr and CONTEXT.md.
agent/plans/
# Exported single-session HTML, megabytes each.
pi-session-*.html

# ---- Logs, scratch and crash output ----------------------------------------
agent/run-history.jsonl
agent/pi-tui-crash.log
herdr.jsonl
*.log
# Loose scratch files from debugging sessions.
g.jsonl
o3.raw

# ---- Local caches -----------------------------------------------------------
agent/fff/
agent/npm/
agent/bin/
agent/git/

# Scratch materialisation of the git index by scripts/check.sh (CHECK_STAGED=1).
.git-check/

# ---- Editor and OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
